WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:02.080
<i>Hey, hey!</i>

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:04.520
Hey, Pop! It's me.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:05.770
<i>Hey, Daigo!</i>

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:06.900
<i>How are you doing?</i>

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:12.030
<i>Oh, your mother told me the Dolphins 
made it to the quarterfinals.</i>

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:17.370
Yeah, our next opponent's the 
team Mayumura's twins play for.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:19.610
<i>So it looks like it's going
 to be a tough game, huh?</i>

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:21.350
Yeah. Really tough.

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.460
But I really want to win!

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:25.580
Which is why I wanted to ask 
your advice on something.

00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:26.170
<i>Oh?</i>

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:27.540
<i>Ask me anything.</i>

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:36.890
I thought they'd throw in their ace, 
but their starting pitcher isn't Mayumura!

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:36.890
Mifune Dolphins

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:36.890
Manager  Tashiro

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:39.760
Komatsu

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:39.760
Komatsu-kun?

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.140
Not their ace?

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.140
Urabe Hayato

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:44.140
Suzuki Andy

00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:43.900
Does this mean they're underestimating us?

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:51.860
Touto Boys

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:51.860
Mayumura Michiru

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:51.860
<i>You're not going to pitch?</i>

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:53.360
Gather round!

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:54.960
All right, let's do this!

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:57.990
Mifune Dolphins

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:57.990
Coach  Fujii

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:09.000
The quarterfinal game between the Mifune
Dolphins and the Touto Boys will now begin!

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:09.900
Bow!

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:11.680
Let's have a good game!

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:48.560
The Touto Match – Play Ball!

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:48.560
So that's Komatsu-kun?

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:51.310
Touto Boys

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:51.310
Pitcher  Komatsu

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:51.310
He's even bigger than Andy.

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:53.020
What are his pitches like?

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.510
No idea.

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:56.860
He must've joined after I left.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.740
Th-That was fast!

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:06.580
He's almost as fast as their ace,
Mayumura Michiru!

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:12.500
What?

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:15.330
I'm not in from the start?

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:17.500
Yeah, change of plan.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:20.000
In their quarterfinal game this morning,

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:22.640
Touto Boys

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:22.640
Manager  Inui

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:22.640
perennial finalists, 
Yokohama Minami, lost.

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:25.020
Yokohama Minami lost?!

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:29.950
Their conquerors, the Nanyou Lions,
look a formidable team.

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:34.920
Our semifinal with them will probably 
end up being the <i>de facto</i> final.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:38.490
Michiru, I want you rested and ready 
for tomorrow's semifinal.

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:41.800
Komatsu can get us through 
today's game with the Dolphins.

00:03:43.270 --> 00:03:48.040
<i>I wanted to face off against 
Shigeno-kun, but what can you do?</i>

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:52.000
Komatsu, don't take any risks 
with the meat of their order.

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:53.500
Touto Boys

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:53.500
Mayumura Wataru

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:56.160
No easy balls for their cleanup, Andy,
and their fifth batter, Satou.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:58.050
We can live with just walking Satou.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:01.800
Don't let their leadoff or two-hole
get on base, though.

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:04.300
Sure, sure.

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:08.810
I-I mean, yessir! Aye, aye, Wakki-san, sir!

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.550
Don't call me that.

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:19.020
<i>Top of the first, and batting first for 
Mifune Dolphins is shortstop, Kimura-kun.</i>

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.650
Shortstop

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:20.650
Kimura

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:20.650
Play ball!

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:26.370
Strike!

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:28.620
Strike two!

00:04:29.520 --> 00:04:31.000
Strike! Out!

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:34.600
Too fast. Couldn't even graze it.

00:04:34.870 --> 00:04:37.790
<i>Batting second, catcher, Shigeno-kun.</i>

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:41.170
Daigo! Good luck!

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:45.260
<i>Shigeno, huh?</i>

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:50.360
<i>With his swing, he'll never be 
able to hit Komatsu's pitches.</i>

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:55.770
<i>I really don't get why he's 
second in their batting order.</i>

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:01.610
Strike!

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:03.150
<i>They really are fast.</i>

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:05.700
<i>I'd never get a hit swinging at them.</i>

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.160
<i>All right, then.</i>

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:12.290
A push bunt!

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:13.000
Michiru!

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:15.910
<i>Did I hit it too far?</i>

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:21.380
Safe!

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:22.250
Awesome!

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.510
Right field

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.510
Sakura Mutsuko

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.510
Pitcher

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:23.510
Satou Hikaru

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:23.510
Nice bunt!

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:26.080
What are you doing, Komatsu?!

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:28.070
And you're heavy! Get off!

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:32.260
I-I'm sorry. Once I'd started running 
to first, it was impossible to stop.

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:37.140
<i>We did make an error, but it 
looks like bunting's his forte.</i>

00:05:38.660 --> 00:05:39.980
<i>That was close.</i>

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:43.120
<i>Batting third, left fielder, Urabe-kun.</i>

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:44.530
Follow it up, Urabe!

00:05:45.590 --> 00:05:48.320
<i>Looks like helping him 
with his bunts paid off.</i>

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:49.700
Play!

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:52.790
Nice bunt. You're not bad, Shigeno-kun.

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:54.900
That totally took us by surprise.

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:56.350
Th-Thanks.

00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:59.710
By the way, have you asked your 
pop about that signed ball?

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:00.350
Huh?

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:03.700
Uh, we're in the middle of a game.
 Can we talk about it after?

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:05.170
Oh, my bad.

00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:08.110
<i>I just told him not to let their leadoff
or two-hole get on base!</i>

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:10.420
<i>Focus on locking this down, Komatsu!</i>

00:06:12.610 --> 00:06:14.810
<i>Micchi smelled really good.</i>

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:18.270
Ow!

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:19.460
HBP!

00:06:19.460 --> 00:06:21.520
All right! The odds of us 
scoring just got better!

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:23.650
Damn, that <i>hurt</i>.

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:25.190
Time out, please.

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:27.570
<i>Oh, crap! Wakki's gonna yell at me.</i>

00:06:27.890 --> 00:06:29.160
<i>That idiot.</i>

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:32.360
Hey! Don't run away!

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:35.040
Please don't yell at me, Wakki-san.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:37.210
I told you not to call me that!

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:41.270
<i>What is it with this team?</i>

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:44.070
<i>Michiru-chan chats to me on first, 
and now, this pitcher...</i>

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:45.780
<i>They're all so relaxed.</i>

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:48.250
<i>Are they laid back 
because they're playing us?</i>

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:50.080
Counting on you, Andy!

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:50.930
Keep us rolling!

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:53.680
<i>Batting fourth, first base, Suzuki-kun.</i>

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:57.060
<i>What? I thought Andy was his last name!</i>

00:06:57.830 --> 00:06:59.930
<i>Don't mess this up, Komatsu.</i>

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:03.140
<i>If you concede a run to these clowns, 
I'll have you subbed out.</i>

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:05.620
<i>Wakki's so scary.</i>

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:09.110
Ball! Ball four!

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:12.160
Yeah!

00:07:12.160 --> 00:07:13.120
All right!

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:15.170
Bases loaded!

00:07:15.170 --> 00:07:16.740
Bases loaded and Hikaru's up next!

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:21.610
<i>Komatsu's really off his game today.</i>

00:07:21.610 --> 00:07:23.960
<i>Because he was thrown in at the last minute,</i>

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:25.900
<i>he hasn't got into his groove yet.</i>

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:27.550
<i>Manager.</i>

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.270
<i>What?!</i>

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:35.950
<i>Michiru?</i>

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:42.270
<i>Batting fifth, pitcher, Satou-kun.</i>

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:44.470
<i>One out, bases loaded.</i>

00:07:45.050 --> 00:07:48.030
<i>We suddenly have a chance 
we didn't even dare dream about!</i>

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:49.830
<i>We're counting on you, Hikaru!</i>

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:51.340
Play!

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:56.490
<i>What?</i>

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:57.530
Strike!

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:01.370
<i>What did Michiru say to Komatsu?</i>

00:08:01.990 --> 00:08:05.220
Sorry about Wataru. I know 
he's always talking down to you.

00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:09.640
He doesn't get just how hard 
it is, being the starting pitcher.

00:08:09.640 --> 00:08:14.110
Anyone'd find it hard to hit the ground
running if they had to start at short notice.

00:08:14.110 --> 00:08:15.640
R-Right.

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:21.270
But if we lose here,
that'll mean the end of our summer.

00:08:21.510 --> 00:08:22.930
Our last summer together...

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:26.710
I want to go to Nationals with you!

00:08:26.710 --> 00:08:28.770
So please, give it all you've got!

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:31.780
Micchi!

00:08:35.090 --> 00:08:35.990
Foul!

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:45.670
Komatsu! Back home!

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:48.840
Out!

00:08:55.350 --> 00:08:56.510
Out!

00:08:58.040 --> 00:09:00.010
Three outs! Change sides!

00:09:00.550 --> 00:09:03.120
Nice block! How's the stomach?

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:07.400
Just fine! I've got some protection 
in that area, after all.

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:11.900
Mifune

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:11.900
Touto

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:09.790
Damn, how unlucky can you get?!

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:11.900
That was such a big opportunity.

00:09:13.180 --> 00:09:14.860
Is something wrong, Hikaru-kun?

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:17.780
Did you hurt yourself sliding?

00:09:18.020 --> 00:09:20.820
Oh, no, I'm fine.

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:24.660
But my dear friend, Mr. Glasses, 
seems to have suffered a serious blow.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:25.970
What?!

00:09:25.970 --> 00:09:27.920
Don't you have a spare pair?!

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:31.040
I do, but they're at home... in Gunma.

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:32.680
Let me take a look.

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:34.050
Nagai

00:09:31.040 --> 00:09:34.050
Tsuburaya

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:38.490
This is bad. The lenses are scratched to hell.

00:09:38.900 --> 00:09:42.350
We can probably fix the frame with some tape,

00:09:43.030 --> 00:09:45.850
but wearing these on the 
mound isn't gonna work.

00:09:46.010 --> 00:09:48.890
Oh! Does this mean I get to start?!

00:09:48.890 --> 00:09:51.910
Hang on a second. What will Satou do?

00:09:51.910 --> 00:09:54.370
If his vision's bad, he can't field.

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:58.050
If anything, the mound's 
probably the best place for him.

00:09:58.580 --> 00:10:03.010
Either way, the starting pitcher 
must throw to at least one batter.

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:07.160
We'll just have to review our options 
once we see what you can do.

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:09.170
Get on the mound, Satou.

00:10:10.070 --> 00:10:10.890
Yes, sir.

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:27.270
Good!

00:10:29.470 --> 00:10:30.610
Is this going to work?

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:34.780
Yeah. It's annoying,
but I think I'll get by somehow.

00:10:35.010 --> 00:10:38.280
<i>Batting first, first base, 
Mayumura Michiru-san.</i>

00:10:40.850 --> 00:10:41.780
Play!

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:43.930
<i>It'll be fine.</i>

00:10:43.930 --> 00:10:47.660
<i>Even Touto won't be able 
to hit Hikaru's pitches easily.</i>

00:10:49.750 --> 00:10:51.960
<i>To be honest, I can't see much...</i>

00:10:52.360 --> 00:10:57.130
<i>but if I know roughly where I'm aiming, 
I'm sure it'll turn out fine!</i>

00:10:59.670 --> 00:11:00.880
Hit by pitch!

00:11:01.310 --> 00:11:02.390
Uh, oops.

00:11:02.580 --> 00:11:04.910
S-Sorry! Are you okay?

00:11:04.910 --> 00:11:08.800
Come on, now!
That better not have been a receipt!

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:10.230
Don't be silly.

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:13.850
<i>Batting second, second base, Hirata-kun.</i>

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:15.850
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:19.360
Second! Second!

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:23.440
All right! Nice running!

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:25.610
A-Are you okay?

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:27.980
Maybe pitching's not possible 
with your glasses like that.

00:11:27.980 --> 00:11:32.320
Hmm... When I was warming up, 
I felt like I could pitch just fine.

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:35.280
I guess I tense up
when there's a batter at the plate,

00:11:35.280 --> 00:11:37.590
so I'll just try to focus on my control.

00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:40.940
If that doesn't work, 
I'll switch with Urabe-kun.

00:11:40.940 --> 00:11:41.890
Okay.

00:11:45.820 --> 00:11:46.640
It got through!

00:11:50.390 --> 00:11:51.480
Michiru, stop!

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:55.560
That was close.

00:11:55.890 --> 00:11:58.030
I forget Urabe-kun was their left fielder.

00:12:00.570 --> 00:12:02.720
You're having a rough time, aren't you, Satou?

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:06.300
Yeah. I tried focusing on my control, but...

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:08.160
Well, we <i>are</i> up against Touto...

00:12:08.610 --> 00:12:10.060
Guess we have no choice.

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:11.570
Um, Manager!

00:12:12.840 --> 00:12:15.290
Instead of giving up hits 
because I'm worried about walks,

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:18.170
I'd like to try throwing at 
full speed one last time!

00:12:20.020 --> 00:12:24.190
If that doesn't take care of the next batter, 
please swap me out for Urabe-kun.

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:27.870
I can't cause the team any more trouble.

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:29.020
Hikaru...

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:31.640
All right.

00:12:32.440 --> 00:12:35.270
<i>Batting third, center field, Yuge-kun.</i>

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:37.430
Is he going to be okay?

00:12:35.650 --> 00:12:39.570
Takahashi

00:12:37.430 --> 00:12:38.670
I don't know.

00:12:38.670 --> 00:12:40.920
But he wanted to pitch to one 
more batter at full speed.

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:42.110
Nagai!

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:44.670
If this doesn't work, 
you'll take over in left field.

00:12:45.330 --> 00:12:47.430
M-Me? Out in left field?

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:55.870
Hikaru!

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:57.410
All right! Straight to the pitcher!

00:12:57.410 --> 00:12:58.130
We can get two out!

00:13:10.390 --> 00:13:12.490
Sweet. We're one run ahead!

00:13:12.490 --> 00:13:14.850
Still no outs, and runners 
on first and second.

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:16.560
Hikaru...

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:20.780
I'm sorry. If I'd just brought 
my spare glasses with me...

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:22.610
Please take care of the rest...

00:13:23.530 --> 00:13:24.550
Hikaru...

00:13:25.430 --> 00:13:27.970
Looks like you're heading out 
to left field, huh, Nagai-kun?

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:29.570
Matsubara

00:13:27.970 --> 00:13:29.570
Y-Yeah...

00:13:30.210 --> 00:13:31.880
Not much we can do, I guess.

00:13:31.880 --> 00:13:33.020
Manager...

00:13:34.300 --> 00:13:35.750
What is it, Nagai?

00:13:38.430 --> 00:13:39.430
Well...

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:50.860
I wonder what happened.

00:13:50.860 --> 00:13:53.060
Aren't they switching their pitchers?

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:56.690
What's going on? I thought 
I was going to take the mound...

00:13:57.520 --> 00:14:00.670
What are you going to do? 
Do you want to switch your pitcher?

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:02.940
No, we won't be switching.

00:14:05.750 --> 00:14:06.650
Hikaru?

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:08.080
Where'd you get the glasses?

00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:09.570
They're Nagai-kun's.

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:11.880
But he doesn't wear glasses...

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:14.410
Nagai-kun wears contacts.

00:14:14.610 --> 00:14:17.470
That's why he had a spare 
pair of glasses with him.

00:14:17.470 --> 00:14:18.810
I see.

00:14:19.950 --> 00:14:23.420
<i>Question is, are they the right strength?</i>

00:14:24.030 --> 00:14:27.420
<i>Batting fourth, catcher, 
Mayumura Wataru-kun.</i>

00:14:29.570 --> 00:14:32.660
<i>If I can see Daigo-kun's mitt this clearly...</i>

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:36.930
<i>nothing's going to hold me back anymore!</i>

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:39.270
Strike!

00:14:40.140 --> 00:14:41.230
Yeah!

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:42.060
All right!

00:14:43.340 --> 00:14:45.430
Nice one!

00:14:45.430 --> 00:14:49.880
Nagai-kun, if you hadn't said anything, 
you could've been out in left field now.

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:51.240
That's true, but...

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:57.370
When I look at those guys,

00:14:57.370 --> 00:15:00.790
I think maybe we <i>do</i> have 
a chance of beating Touto.

00:15:02.380 --> 00:15:04.170
I'm a dope, aren't I?

00:15:05.970 --> 00:15:06.920
Nagai.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:11.090
I appreciate that you stepped 
up in our hour of need.

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:13.370
Sure.

00:15:14.400 --> 00:15:16.550
<i>So they've resolved their issues.</i>

00:15:16.950 --> 00:15:22.350
<i>Okay. It'd be no fun if I didn't use my bat 
to knock you out for the count, anyway!</i>

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:27.360
Strike two!

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:28.820
<i>All right!</i>

00:15:31.980 --> 00:15:36.490
<i>One run behind, runners on first and 
second. I can't let them score again!</i>

00:15:40.820 --> 00:15:42.000
Foul!

00:15:42.190 --> 00:15:43.940
<i>He can already hit them?</i>

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:46.370
<i>You throw some good balls.</i>

00:15:46.850 --> 00:15:50.200
<i>They're so lively that I even
swung late on the second pitch.</i>

00:15:50.620 --> 00:15:51.500
<i>However...</i>

00:15:54.230 --> 00:15:58.630
<i>I've already analyzed 
your pitching thoroughly.</i>

00:15:59.750 --> 00:16:04.650
<i>No matter how fast they are, your pitches
always come in straight. Your pitches...</i>

00:16:12.870 --> 00:16:13.990
Right field!

00:16:15.410 --> 00:16:16.490
Foul!

00:16:17.650 --> 00:16:20.750
<i>...are easy enough to hit if I have
one at bat to get my eye in.</i>

00:16:21.350 --> 00:16:22.990
Aw, so close.

00:16:22.990 --> 00:16:25.530
<i>Wataru's already got his number 
in his first at bat.</i>

00:16:25.530 --> 00:16:28.800
<i>I was expecting much better 
things from you, Satou Hikaru.</i>

00:16:32.240 --> 00:16:34.300
A way to improve your control?

00:16:34.750 --> 00:16:35.720
Yes.

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:37.800
With my unreliable control,

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:40.410
I probably won't be able to do 
much against Touto's offense.

00:16:41.060 --> 00:16:43.520
I need to be able to hit targets.

00:16:43.520 --> 00:16:48.470
You know it's impossible to gain that 
much control in just a week, right?

00:16:48.470 --> 00:16:50.690
I know, but it doesn't hurt to try.

00:16:50.690 --> 00:16:54.570
Hmm, I guess I'll ask Pop, then.

00:16:54.970 --> 00:16:58.380
Maybe he'll know a training 
method that'll help you out.

00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:08.460
Strike! Out!

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:09.680
What?

00:17:09.680 --> 00:17:10.380
He did it!

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:12.800
He struck out their cleanup!

00:17:13.130 --> 00:17:14.310
Nice ball!

00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:19.910
What happened? I thought 
you had him all figured out.

00:17:19.910 --> 00:17:21.220
I don't know.

00:17:21.630 --> 00:17:24.430
He's not supposed to have that much control.

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:28.440
For some reason, that last pitch
was right on the outside corner.

00:17:28.680 --> 00:17:30.270
Maybe it was just coincidence.

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:32.360
I sure hope so.

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:35.140
Strike! Out!

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:37.360
Mifune

00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:37.360
Touto

00:17:35.140 --> 00:17:37.090
Three outs! Change sides!

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:38.330
All right!

00:17:38.330 --> 00:17:41.660
From no outs, runners on first and 
second, to three strikeouts in a row!

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:43.710
Nice pitching, Hikaru!

00:17:45.780 --> 00:17:48.290
That speccy kid ain't bad, after all.

00:17:49.060 --> 00:17:52.960
Listen up! No fooling around 
like you did in the first inning.

00:17:53.320 --> 00:17:56.710
This might end up being a low score game.

00:17:57.220 --> 00:17:59.840
Since we don't know how 
many runs we'll get off Satou,

00:17:59.840 --> 00:18:02.390
defend with the mindset that 
we need to maintain our 1-0 lead.

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:03.750
Got it.

00:18:05.870 --> 00:18:07.310
Strike! Out!

00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:09.810
Mifune

00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:09.810
Touto

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:09.390
Three outs! Change sides!

00:18:12.580 --> 00:18:14.070
Strike! Out!

00:18:15.600 --> 00:18:17.070
Strike! Out!

00:18:18.250 --> 00:18:19.630
Strike! Out!

00:18:19.630 --> 00:18:21.540
Three outs! Change sides!

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:22.580
Mifune

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:22.580
Touto

00:18:23.000 --> 00:18:24.300
I can't believe this.

00:18:24.300 --> 00:18:26.180
They're actually making us play.

00:18:26.610 --> 00:18:27.560
I figured it out.

00:18:27.560 --> 00:18:28.290
What?

00:18:29.270 --> 00:18:32.290
The trick behind his pitching.

00:18:33.020 --> 00:18:35.760
We can dismantle it when you're next at bat.

00:18:36.840 --> 00:18:39.550
<i>Batting ninth, right field, Sakura-san.</i>

00:18:39.550 --> 00:18:42.150
<i>Oh, they had a girl on their team?</i>

00:18:42.150 --> 00:18:44.220
<i>I'll let her get a hit 'cause she's cute.</i>

00:18:44.740 --> 00:18:46.850
<i>As if I'd do something like that!</i>

00:18:48.600 --> 00:18:49.600
What?!

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:53.230
All right!

00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:53.690
Well done!

00:18:55.160 --> 00:18:57.120
<i>This girl has a nice swing.</i>

00:18:57.320 --> 00:19:00.820
<i>Komatsu! You went easy on her
because she's a girl!</i>

00:19:02.390 --> 00:19:05.160
<i>Batting first, shortstop, Kimura-kun.</i>

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:09.570
<i>Uh oh. If they get a runner on second
for their cleanup,</i>

00:19:09.570 --> 00:19:11.460
<i>Wakki's gonna yell at me again.</i>

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:16.460
Wai—

00:19:19.720 --> 00:19:20.520
All right!

00:19:20.000 --> 00:19:20.920
Sweet!

00:19:20.520 --> 00:19:22.680
No outs, and a runner on second!

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:31.760
Nice bunt!

00:19:31.760 --> 00:19:33.920
Great! One out, and a runner on third!

00:19:34.780 --> 00:19:37.770
<i>Batting second, catcher, Shigeno-kun.</i>

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:41.530
Ball!

00:19:45.730 --> 00:19:47.290
<i>I'm counting on you, Daigo!</i>

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:50.790
It's a squeeze play!

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:53.100
What?!

00:19:53.100 --> 00:19:54.130
They're bypassing him!

00:20:03.270 --> 00:20:04.300
We did it!

00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:05.220
We're tied!

00:20:05.220 --> 00:20:06.470
Nice one, Daigo-kun!

00:20:07.020 --> 00:20:08.010
Out!

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:13.440
All your training's paid off, Daigo!

00:20:13.640 --> 00:20:16.610
I-I'm sorry. Was that my fault?

00:20:16.610 --> 00:20:21.650
No. We put it in an area it would've
been hard to hit with your speed.

00:20:22.210 --> 00:20:24.880
But he still managed not to foul the ball.

00:20:24.880 --> 00:20:29.720
I should've been more wary of his bunts
 after his display in the first inning.

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:33.040
All right. Time to follow it up!

00:20:34.970 --> 00:20:35.920
Out!

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:39.130
Mifune

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:39.130
Touto

00:20:36.910 --> 00:20:38.830
Three outs! Change sides!

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:41.340
All right! We've caught up! We can do this!

00:20:41.340 --> 00:20:42.220
Yeah!

00:20:42.220 --> 00:20:47.020
Hey, maybe we really <i>can</i> do this. 
We might witness a miracle!

00:20:47.020 --> 00:20:50.200
No, it's still way too early to 
start counting our chickens.

00:20:51.010 --> 00:20:54.870
The Touto Boys haven't shown
any sign of being rattled.

00:20:56.720 --> 00:20:57.650
Michiru.

00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:00.900
What?

00:21:02.710 --> 00:21:09.740
<i>Bottom of the third, batting first for 
the Touto Boys, Mayumura Michiru-san.</i>

00:21:11.280 --> 00:21:12.250
<i>Are you kidding me?</i>

00:21:13.130 --> 00:21:17.250
<i>The secret to his newfound control
is something so simple?</i>

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:21.420
Strike!

00:21:22.420 --> 00:21:23.640
It's true!

00:21:24.030 --> 00:21:26.440
<i>We're going to play seriously now.</i>

00:21:27.010 --> 00:21:30.740
<i>It's time you stopped believing 
we're on the same level.</i>

00:21:39.140 --> 00:21:40.020
It got through!

00:21:40.870 --> 00:21:43.030
Their leadoff got a double.

00:21:46.360 --> 00:21:48.990
All Satou's doing to change 
the direction of his pitches

00:21:49.860 --> 00:21:51.670
is stepping on different 
parts of the rubber.

00:21:53.010 --> 00:21:56.760
If his foot's closer to third, 
it's going to the outside for a lefty.

00:21:57.280 --> 00:21:59.150
If it's closer to first, it's the inside.

00:21:59.150 --> 00:22:00.290
That's all there is to it.

00:22:01.600 --> 00:22:05.580
<i>No matter how fast the pitch is, 
if we know where the ball's going,</i>

00:22:05.580 --> 00:22:08.000
<i>we've basically defanged him.</i>

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:13.800
Hikaru, she stepped inside 
to hit that outside ball.

00:22:13.800 --> 00:22:15.680
It's possible they've figured it out.

00:22:15.680 --> 00:22:16.450
Huh?

00:22:19.040 --> 00:22:19.770
I see.

00:22:20.770 --> 00:22:23.260
Well, if that won't fly anymore, 
we'll use our next trick.

00:22:23.950 --> 00:22:25.530
I've still got plenty up my sleeve.

00:24:01.210 --> 00:24:02.000
Crap.

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:04.210
They figured out the 
secret to Hikaru's pitches!

00:24:05.170 --> 00:24:07.350
Touto's fearsome lineup bare their fangs.

00:24:07.350 --> 00:24:10.030
Damn it! I'm not giving up!

00:24:10.620 --> 00:24:12.550
Please, Hikaru, hang in there!

00:24:13.050 --> 00:24:16.350
We'll get out of this tight spot and play
catch up as many times as we need to!

00:24:16.750 --> 00:24:19.100
We will... Won't we, Hikaru?

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:25.020
Daigo and Hikaru!

00:24:19.780 --> 00:24:22.250
Next time: "Daigo and Hikaru!"

00:24:22.250 --> 00:24:24.290
Run to the stage of your dreams!
